WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.330
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:09.540
With the recent ascendancy of several new
AI-based techniques for human facial reenactment,

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.540
we are now able to create videos where we
transfer our gestures onto famous actors or

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.910
politicians and impersonate them.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:21.480
Clearly, as this only needs a few minutes
of video as training data from the target,

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.970
this could be super useful for animating photorealistic
characters for video games and movies, reviving

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:30.980
legendary actors who are not with us anymore,
and much more.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.290
And understandably, some are worried about
the social implications of such a powerful

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.290
tool.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:41.470
In other words, if there are tools to create
forgery, there should be tools to detect forgery,

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:42.470
right?

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:48.080
If we can train an AI to impersonate, why
not train an other AI to detect impersonation?

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.600
This has to be an arms race.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.820
However, this is no easy task to say the least.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.690
As an example, look here.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:57.760
Some of these faces are real, some are fake.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.390
What do you think, which is which?

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:04.600
I will have to admit, my guesses weren't all
that great.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:05.600
But what about you?

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.510
Let me know in the comments section.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.240
Compression is also an issue.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.350
Since all videos you see here on YouTube are
compressed in some way to reduce filesize,

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:19.750
some of the artifacts that appear may easily
throw off not only an AI, but a human as well.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:24.600
I bet there will be many completely authentic
videos that will be thought of as fakes by

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.340
humans in the near future.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.980
So how do we solve these problems?

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:33.270
First, to obtain a neural network-based solution,
we need a large dataset to train it on.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:38.390
This paper contains a useful dataset with
over a 1000 videos that we can use to train

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.060
such a neural network.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:45.350
These records contain pairs of original and
manipulated videos, along with the input footage

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.260
of the gestures that were transferred.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:51.620
After the training step, the algorithm will
be able to pick up on the smallest changes

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:57.510
around the face and tell a forged footage
from a real one, even in cases where we humans

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.240
are unable to do that.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.110
This is really amazing.

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:05.940
These green to red colors showcase regions
that the AI thinks were tampered with.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.299
And it is correct.

00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:12.010
Interestingly, this can not only identify
regions that are forgeries, but it can also

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.989
improve these forgeries too.

00:02:13.989 --> 00:02:18.020
I wonder if it can detect footage that is
has improved itself?

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.020
What do you think?

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.479
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

